    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jacob Wilson** (71.63) and **Drake Baldwin** (70.05) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from high-leverage spots at the top of the order against favorable SP_xERA matchups. **Jacob Wilson** is particularly well-positioned today; his 10% park boost and prime leadoff placement against Valdez yield our highest efficiency score. **Jackson Merrill** (69.24) also stands out as an elite play; despite a neutral matchup against Mahle, his dynamic platoon edge (+13%) makes him a high-floor producer. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.59) continues to defy potential platoon concerns, providing essential stability in the cleanup-adjacent #2 spot as he maximizes park factors to stay well within our \"Strong\" start threshold.\n\nNavigating the peripheral matchups required difficult decisions, particularly regarding our middle infield and outfield depth. **Nasim Nunez** (60.14) provides a critical speed boost, holding his spot despite a suboptimal #7 order placement, while **Dominic Smith** (59.78) maintains value through a platoon advantage against Mikolas. The most difficult exclusion was **Denzer Guzman** (44.36), who was the first cut from the active roster; while his profile is trending upward, he fell just short of the efficiency baseline compared to **Sam Antonacci** (45.19), whose leadoff volume ultimately secured his spot in the OF. We are closely monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** (49.62) and **Coby Mayo** (52.59); both face a rigorous challenge against the sub-3.00 xERA of S\u00e1nchez. Their scores are suppressed by the elite nature of the opposing arm, but their talent levels necessitate the start despite the elevated risk of a suppressed offensive output. With **Kyle Tucker** and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined, roster flexibility remains tight, and we are proceeding without additional injury concerns as of this morning\u2019s report.",
